Description: Keel overlay: etcd, the mesh registry
 The etcd overlay of Keel Linux (handbook decisions 0025 and 0036): trixie's
 etcd-server, its etcdctl (etcd-client, the same upstream version), which
 keel asks etcd with over gRPC (keel#83), and the overlay manifest keel
 reads, installed as /usr/share/keel/overlays/etcd.yaml (decision 0041).
 .
 etcd is installed disabled and stopped, the state of a simple
 installation: the first installation of this package disables the unit
 etcd-server's own maintainer scripts enabled, and a systemd preset keeps
 it disabled at first boot. keel spec apply turns it on where the instance
 spec says so. On a running system where etcd was already enabled or
 running before this package, it is left as it was; an image build always
 ends with it disabled.
 .
 A drop-in of etcd.service restarts etcd one member at a time: before it
 stops, keel mesh etcd gate waits until every other member is healthy and
 none restarts, so an upgrade of etcd-server on several members at once
 never loses the cluster's majority.
